      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes how the guarded tool executor safeguards file writes with all-or-nothing semantics:\n\nBefore any file is overwritten, the system records its prior state into an in-memory write journal \u2014 either the file\u0027s previous content or a note that it didn\u0027t exist. If the agent run fails for any reason (turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content where files existed, or deleting newly created files. This provides transaction-like atomicity without needing a database.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent (the one querying this wiki) never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool \u2014 only agents that actually write to files use the journal\u0027s rollback functionality.",
